\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Family-level DQN--MPC-4 evidence in the synthetic soft-constrained benchmark. (a) Six DQN objectives and MPC-4 are evaluated in 20 paired model-seed blocks, each averaging 20 shared held-out traces. (b) Cells report the mean episode-cost difference, DQN minus MPC-4, for all 30 objective--regime contrasts; negative values favor DQN. (c) Circles and lines show the largest, least-favorable mean difference within each scope and its 95\% joint-bootstrap interval; open triangles show simultaneous 95\% upper bounds. A single 10,000-resample seed-block bootstrap preserves correlation among the 30 contrasts. Exact two-sided sign tests are Holm-adjusted across all 30 comparisons, all of which satisfy the prespecified support rule.\relax }}{2}{figure.caption.1}\protected@file@percent }
\providecommand*\caption@xref[2]{\@setref\relax\@undefined{#1}}
\newlabel{fig:graphical}{{1}{2}{Family-level DQN--MPC-4 evidence in the synthetic soft-constrained benchmark. (a) Six DQN objectives and MPC-4 are evaluated in 20 paired model-seed blocks, each averaging 20 shared held-out traces. (b) Cells report the mean episode-cost difference, DQN minus MPC-4, for all 30 objective--regime contrasts; negative values favor DQN. (c) Circles and lines show the largest, least-favorable mean difference within each scope and its 95\% joint-bootstrap interval; open triangles show simultaneous 95\% upper bounds. A single 10,000-resample seed-block bootstrap preserves correlation among the 30 contrasts. Exact two-sided sign tests are Holm-adjusted across all 30 comparisons, all of which satisfy the prespecified support rule.\relax }{figure.caption.1}{}}
